  <h2>Is a scissor cut the right service for you?</h2>
  <p>A scissor cut is worth discussing when you want to retain length, shape layers, or keep a softer outline. The best service choice depends on the result you want, not just the tool used. If your reference photo combines a longer top with closely tapered sides, ask which appointment to select before booking.</p>
  <p>For shorter styles and fade options, explore our <a href="/mens-haircut-richmond-va/">men's haircut service</a>.</p>
  <h2>Bring a clear reference</h2>
  <p>Bring photos showing the front, sides, and back of a style you like. Tell your barber which parts you want to keep, how much length you are comfortable losing, and how you normally style your hair. That gives the conversation a practical starting point.</p>
  <h2>Keeping length while changing the shape</h2>
  <p>Growing your hair out does not mean every appointment needs to be a major change. Explain where you want more length and where the shape feels heavy.</p>
  <h2>Prices and appointment availability</h2>
  <p>Select Scissor Cut in our booking menu to see current pricing and available times. If you are unsure which service fits your haircut, call the shop before choosing your appointment.</p>
</ServiceDetailLayout>
